      "Anemia (iron deficiency or chronic disease): Can produce progressive exertional dyspnea and fatigue, potentially aggravating heart failure symptoms.",
      "Progressive decline in cardiac function (ischemic/degenerative cardiomyopathy): Worsening systolic dysfunction over time can present as gradual dyspnea and edema."
    ],
    "I2": [
      "Inadequate diuretic dosing/nonadherence or diuretic resistance: Patient is on furosemide (dose unknown); subtherapeutic dosing or decreased response could lead to volume overload and worsening dyspnea/edema.",
